      "value": "@{5af78181852432465920134e|full_name}: I do understand where your coming from but, I like to think from a completely different perspective.\nIf software is exploitable, someone will find a way to exploit it, the best way to fight exploits is to harden your software and listen to bug reports from members of the community.\nIts why I like the opensource approach to development.\nIf people where able to self host, yes that would give malicious actors an easier way to experiment with exploits, it would also give legitimate community members/modders/ avatar and world devs the ability to report these exploits before they become widespread on public servers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
