      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would like to request/suggest the implementation of support for self-hosted servers in VRChat. (As this feedback is already asking)\n\nThis feature aims to improve the experience of players who face high latencies (above 160ms) due to the distance from official servers.\n\nJustification:\n\nCurrently, players in regions far from official servers face significant difficulties in interacting fluidly within VRChat. This compromises the quality of the social and immersive experience, especially in instances with a large number of participants. High ping causes noticeable delays in avatar movements, voice communication (VOIP) and general synchronization within worlds.\n\nProposal:\n\nWe suggest implementing an option so that users can host servers dedicated exclusively to handle:\n\nMovement of avatars within the world of the created instance;\n\nText and voice communication (VOIP);\n\nThis server would have no other function besides these, ensuring that the game infrastructure remains secure and controlled by VRChat. To facilitate access, players could connect to the self-hosted server by simply entering its IP and port when creating or joining an instance in the world.\n\nBenefits:\n\nSignificantly reduced ping for players in remote regions, improving the overall experience;\n\nImproved fluidity in avatar movement, reducing delays and synchronization;\n\nMore responsive voice communication, ensuring more natural interactions;\n\nGreater accessibility for international communities, allowing local groups to have a more optimized experience without relying exclusively on official servers;\n\nReduced load on official servers, as part of the processing would be decentralized.\n\nWe believe that this proposal would bring considerable improvement to the community and enable a more inclusive experience for players around the world. We look forward to your attention.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
